claimed: okay-script-meta -- code inside an .md file gets access to the metadata defined in the markup AROUND it, as a current context (operator, 2026-09-03). Source of metadata: YAML front-matter (---...---) at the top of the file (file-level) plus nested ```yaml fenced blocks, scoped by heading (# / ## / ###) ancestry -- code physically under a heading sees that heading's own yaml plus every ANCESTOR heading's yaml plus the front-matter, nearest wins on a shared key. New module okay.script.Meta: a typed AST (Value = Str|Arr|Obj, Section(level,title,yaml,children), Doc(frontMatter,root)) built by a minimal YAML-subset parser (flat mapping, and a list of flat mappings -- the shape already seen in ../it-consulting/site/site.md's own services yaml), plus Context(doc,path) with untyped get/apply AND the full typed Doc for tree navigation. Exposed to BOTH run and render (a property of the file, not of which mode compiles it) via an injected local `given Meta.Context` re-declared at each heading-boundary transition in document order, literalized directly as Scala source (no runtime re-parsing needed by the compiled script). ```yaml fences become metadata (consumed, not shown in render output) -- a deliberate, documented change from the prior any-non-scala-fence-passes-through-verbatim rule, specific to yaml.
